#: ../../source/templates_expo.md:16
msgid "1. Visual Theme & Atmosphere"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_expo.md:18
msgid ""
"Expo's interface is a luminous, confidence-radiating developer platform "
"built on the premise that tools for building apps should feel as polished"
" as the apps themselves. The entire experience lives on a bright, airy "
"canvas — a cool-tinted off-white (`#f0f0f3`) that gives the page a subtle"
" technological coolness without the starkness of pure white. This is a "
"site that breathes: enormous vertical spacing between sections creates a "
"gallery-like pace where each feature gets its own \"room.\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_expo.md:20
msgid ""
"The design language is decisively monochromatic — pure black (`#000000`) "
"headlines against the lightest possible backgrounds, with a spectrum of "
"cool blue-grays (`#60646c`, `#b0b4ba`, `#555860`) handling all secondary "
"communication. Color is almost entirely absent from the interface itself;"
" when it appears, it's reserved for product screenshots, app icons, and "
"the React universe illustration — making the actual content burst with "
"life against the neutral canvas."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_expo.md:22
msgid ""
"What makes Expo distinctive is its pill-shaped geometry. Buttons, tabs, "
"video containers, and even images use generously rounded or fully pill-"
"shaped corners (24px–9999px), creating an organic, approachable feel that"
" contradicts the typical sharp-edged developer tool aesthetic. Combined "
"with tight letter-spacing on massive headlines (-1.6px to -3px at 64px), "
"the result is a design that's simultaneously premium and friendly — like "
"an Apple product page reimagined for developers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_expo.md:24
msgid "**Key Characteristics:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_expo.md:25
msgid "Luminous cool-white canvas (`#f0f0f3`) with gallery-like vertical spacing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_expo.md:26
msgid ""
"Strictly monochromatic: pure black headlines, cool blue-gray body text, "
"no decorative color"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_expo.md:27
msgid ""
"Pill-shaped geometry everywhere — buttons, tabs, containers, images "
"(24px–9999px radius)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_expo.md:28
msgid ""
"Massive display headlines (64px) with extreme negative letter-spacing "
"(-1.6px to -3px)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_expo.md:29
msgid ""
"Inter as the sole typeface, used at weights 400–900 for full expressive "
"range"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_expo.md:30
msgid "Whisper-soft shadows that barely lift elements from the surface"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_expo.md:31
msgid "Product screenshots as the only source of color in the interface"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_expo.md:33
msgid "2. Color Palette & Roles"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_expo.md:35
msgid "Primary"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_expo.md:36
msgid ""
"**Expo Black** (`#000000`): The absolute anchor — used for primary "
"headlines, CTA buttons, and the brand identity. Pure black on cool white "
"creates maximum contrast without feeling aggressive."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_expo.md:37
msgid ""
"**Near Black** (`#1c2024`): The primary text color for body content — a "
"barely perceptible blue-black that's softer than pure #000 for extended "
"reading."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_expo.md:39
msgid "Secondary & Accent"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_expo.md:40
msgid ""
"**Link Cobalt** (`#0d74ce`): The standard link color — a trustworthy, "
"saturated blue that signals interactivity without competing with the "
"monochrome hierarchy."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_expo.md:41
msgid ""
"**Legal Blue** (`#476cff`): A brighter, more saturated blue for "
"legal/footer links — slightly more attention-grabbing than Link Cobalt."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_expo.md:42
msgid ""
"**Widget Sky** (`#47c2ff`): A light, friendly cyan-blue for widget "
"branding elements — the brightest accent in the system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_expo.md:43
msgid ""
"**Preview Purple** (`#8145b5`): A rich violet used for \"preview\" or "
"beta feature indicators — creating clear visual distinction from standard"
" content."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_expo.md:45
msgid "Surface & Background"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_expo.md:46
msgid ""
"**Cloud Gray** (`#f0f0f3`): The primary page background — a cool off-"
"white with the faintest blue-violet tint. Not warm, not sterile — "
"precisely technological."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_expo.md:47
msgid ""
"**Pure White** (`#ffffff`): Card surfaces, button backgrounds, and "
"elevated content containers. Creates a clear \"lifted\" distinction from "
"Cloud Gray."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_expo.md:48
msgid ""
"**Widget Dark** (`#1a1a1a`): Dark surface for dark-theme widgets and "
"overlay elements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_expo.md:49
msgid ""
"**Banner Dark** (`#171717`): The darkest surface variant, used for "
"promotional banners and high-contrast containers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_expo.md:51
msgid "Neutrals & Text"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_expo.md:52
msgid ""
"**Slate Gray** (`#60646c`): The workhorse secondary text color (305 "
"instances). A cool blue-gray that's authoritative without being heavy."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_expo.md:53
msgid ""
"**Mid Slate** (`#555860`): Slightly darker than Slate, used for "
"emphasized secondary text."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_expo.md:54
msgid ""
"**Silver** (`#b0b4ba`): Tertiary text, placeholders, and de-emphasized "
"metadata. Comfortably readable but clearly receded."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_expo.md:55
msgid ""
"**Pewter** (`#999999`): Accordion icons and deeply de-emphasized UI "
"elements in dark contexts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_expo.md:56
msgid ""
"**Light Silver** (`#cccccc`): Arrow icons and decorative elements in dark"
" contexts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_expo.md:57
msgid ""
"**Dark Slate** (`#363a3f`): Borders on dark surfaces, switch tracks, and "
"emphasized containment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_expo.md:58
msgid ""
"**Charcoal** (`#333333`): Dark mode switch backgrounds and deep secondary"
" surfaces."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_expo.md:60
msgid "Semantic & Accent"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_expo.md:61
msgid ""
"**Warning Amber** (`#ab6400`): A warm, deep amber for warning states — "
"deliberately not bright yellow, conveying seriousness."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_expo.md:62
msgid ""
"**Destructive Rose** (`#eb8e90`): A soft pink-coral for disabled "
"destructive actions — gentler than typical red, reducing alarm fatigue."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_expo.md:63
msgid ""
"**Border Lavender** (`#e0e1e6`): Standard card/container borders — a cool"
" lavender-gray that's visible without being heavy."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_expo.md:64
msgid ""
"**Input Border** (`#d9d9e0`): Button and form element borders — slightly "
"warmer/darker than card borders for interactive elements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_expo.md:65
msgid ""
"**Dark Focus Ring** (`#2547d0`): Deep blue for keyboard focus indicators "
"in dark theme contexts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_expo.md:67
msgid "Gradient System"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_expo.md:68
msgid ""
"The design is notably **gradient-free** in the interface layer. Visual "
"richness comes from product screenshots, the React universe illustration,"
" and careful shadow layering rather than color gradients. This absence IS"
" the design decision — gradients would undermine the clinical precision."
msgstr ""

